==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Bring at least 3 meatshields but 4 is highly recommended. Any DPS units you bring should definitely outrange Cadaver bear who sits at 360 range with an attack every .66 seconds. Again, bring as many Zombie Killer units as possible with units that can freeze Cadaver Bear getting special mention due to how much pressure is relieved from a frozen C. Bear.

Stack up a couple cat worker levels early but be ready to shield the Imperator Sael that spawns then dump everything you've got on the Bear and Zuche after they burrow.

Cadaver Bear deals a monster amount of damage, attacks non-stop like assassin bear and will revive with 100% hp. Bring long range nukers and freeze him if you can to help reduce his damage even further.

The One Horn provides a very large amount of cash so the earlier it dies the better, but your team may get separated due to the bear burrowing and the One Horn being very slow.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Similar strategy as chapter 1. Prepare for the double burrow by trying to save up a lot of cash early.

The boss duo doesn't have too much health, but they attack very fast and can prove to be a deadly combo. Keep in mind that Zuche and Cadaver Bear revive with 100% HP instead of 50% and Zuche will revive after what seems like '''FOREVER''', giving your cats ample time to move forward and leave your base extremely vulnerable.

Longer ranged Zombie Killer cats are again a great choice for this stage as are any units you have that Freeze zombies, especially with the addition of Zuche.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The major change between this stage and the previous ZO are the Cyberhorn walls that will constantly spawn and slow you down. Add a couple of Zuches and a Cadaver Bear, that really wants to get behind your DPS line and smack your base... This level could give you trouble.

A decent split between zombie and alien cats will be needed to make this one work. Mainly to kill Zuche/Cadaver Bear as quickly as possible in the back lines while being able to keep Cyberhorn and permaslow Imperator from breaking your meatshield line. Any instance of Freeze, weaken or slow will be helpful here.

Save a heavy hitting zombie killer for after Cadaver bear spawns so he doesn't pummel your base. You can also try to time the cat cannon to knock him out of burrow but honestly its easier and more useful against Zuche as he attacks a lot faster.

Cyberhorn will start to hurt a lot if he gets close to your base. Don't let him push if you can. This means bringing strong anti-alien meatshields like [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] with the Target Alien talent.

Its a long-slow trek to the enemy base with zombie enemies constantly wanting to kill your dps and Ubers. Protect them well!

